## 6. Open on-hardware verification — Verification Only

No code changes. Six checks that cannot be run without the unit:

| Check | Pass criterion |
|---|---|
| Flash & boot | Device boots, first evaluation logged |
| Autonomy | HA stopped → SNTP time valid, AUTO evaluations continue, correct day/night profile, web-GUI mode changes take effect |
| Persistence | Power-cycle in HOOG → boots into HOOG; cleared restore → AUTO |
| Fail-safe | I²C disconnected → FAULT within `staleness_timeout_ms`, fan 15 %, clean recovery |
| HA entity_ids | All four presentation sensors unchanged across the v1.0 → v2.0.0 filter split |
| Tacho calibration | RPM logged at commanded 0/15/25/30/35/40/55/85 % |

Notes: the autonomy and persistence checks should be re-run **after** items 1
and 2 land, since both touch exactly those paths. The tacho calibration pass is
a prerequisite for any future commanded-vs-actual RPM band check and a
`fan_fault` entity — neither is in scope here; record the data only.

